;; A BROAD PROBE OF THE JAVASCRIPT SURFACE, for `tools/js-sweep.coil` to enumerate.
;;
;; SEPARATE FROM `js_templates.coil` ON PURPOSE, and the reason is the difference between a
;; property and a sweep.
;;
;; `tests/js-source-prop.coil` SHRINKS. A body it cannot lower poisons a large share of every
;; generated case, the shrinker converges on it, and the property reports that one known failure
;; for ever instead of exploring -- so every template there has to be pre-validated against node
;; AND against the frontend, and docs/FUZZ-FINDINGS.md records each time one was bent around an
;; open defect.
;;
;; The sweep CATALOGUES. It runs a fixed matrix, prints one line per case, and never minimises or
;; stops, so a body that fails is a finding rather than a poison -- and a body that fails in fifty
;; combinations is one catalogue entry with a count of fifty. That inverts the discipline: probes
;; here are DELIBERATELY unvalidated, because a probe that already works teaches nothing.
;;
;; The contract each probe still owes is composition: read the integer accumulator `acc`, write it,
;; touch nothing else. That is what makes any sequence of any probes a valid program, so the sweep
;; needs no rejection filter and a pair that fails is genuinely about the pair.
;;
;; A probe that earns its place -- one that finds something, gets it fixed, and then passes -- is
;; worth promoting into `js_templates.coil` so the property explores it too.
(module jsprobes)

(import "coil.control" :use *)
(import "coil.fmt" :use *)
(import "coil.io" :use *)
(import "coil.slice" :use *)

(defn js-probe-count [] (-> i64)
  169)

